I go to the next stall.
There are many types of cheese there.
A trader is cutting large wheels of cheese.
He sees me and smiles.
"Would you like to taste a piece?" he asks.
"Yes, very gladly," I say.
He hands me a piece of cheese on a small wooden stick.
I taste the cheese.
It is spicy and extremely delicious.
"I will take a large piece, please," I say.
"How much does that cost?"
The trader weighs the cheese.
"That makes eight euros fifty," he says.
I give him ten euros.
He gives me one euro fifty back.
The trader wraps the cheese in paper.
He gives me my piece of cheese and the receipt.
I put the cheese into my shopping bag.
"Have a nice weekend!" calls the trader.
"Thank you, you too!" I answer and walk on.
